etimes like throw on a little workout  app or a youtube video for some quick  little sets i personally love sydney  cummings workouts the best and honestly  sometimes i can only fit in like 10  minutes here and 15 minutes there and  that's great too like it doesn't always  have to be a big workout all at once i  generally take at least two days off of  doing any resistance training at all but  i still do try to move my body when i  get the chance i admittedly don't run  because hashtag childbirth i literally  had prolapse and my diastasis recti  still has not made it very easy for me  to even like chase after my kid on a  bike but i do try to get some walking in  most days otherwise i just find myself  sitting down at my desk or in front of  the camera all day and it just doesn't  feel good to my body physical health  aside i really find walking to be very  helpful for my mental health and for my  digestion if i'm feeling bloated or  gassy or backed up i will go for a walk  if i'm feeling particularly anxious i go  for a walk if i'm having terrible  insomnia sometimes i get out of my bed  and i go for a quick little walk to  reset my brain i am naturally a very  busy body it's just what comes with my  personality so i've never been good at  sitting down and meditating but this  feels like a bit of a walking meditation  to me and i definitely find it's helpful  i also get about 30 minutes in daily  just walking my kid to and from school  every day and i try to take my zoom  calls walking outside or on the  treadmill if it's not a super nice day  my team has basically come to expect to  hear the treadmill buzz in the  background on most of our calls because  that might be the only chance that i get  to actually move that day but now let's  talk about my post-workout meal all  right so for a quick little post workout  i'm going to throw together what i have  already in the fridge and make a really  fast easy quesadilla and a little salad  combo on the side for my lunch